C03: the Steam library final names the game without the word «título» (INSTALL1619)

INSTALL1617 measured that game.entitlement.named is decided, completed and verified for the Steam download, install and uninstall rows, and that the model drafts the intended final («<juego> no está en tu biblioteca, así que no puedes descargarlo ni instalarlo»), but the composer's generic title check rejected every draft with missing_name: a payload that carries `title` demanded the word «título» in the sentence. A verified library read is now exempt from that word, as the local YouTube playback already is: naming the game is what the sentence owes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


